Patch: OpenGLide-ng SDL window handle width
Upstream: https://github.com/eugenenuke/openglide-ng at the commit named by BACKEND in tools/package_native.py; applied by tools/build_linux.py.
Original: on 64-bit builds InitialiseOpenGLWindow assumes a window handle is a 32-bit value and takes the 32-bit path for foreign window ids.
Replacement: the 64-bit path is skipped when RG_SDL_WINDOW_POINTER is defined, so the handle passed in is used as the SDL window pointer.
Effect: with RG_SDL_WINDOW_POINTER the renderer draws into the window the Rust runtime created instead of misreading its pointer.
Why: the runtime creates the SDL window and hands its pointer to the renderer.
Evidence: glide/bridge.cpp; the Glide window checks in the Linux run.

diff --git a/platform/sdl/window.cpp b/platform/sdl/window.cpp
--- a/platform/sdl/window.cpp
+++ b/platform/sdl/window.cpp
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
         self_wnd = (window)? true:false;
     }
     else {
-#if (SIZEOF_INT_P == 8)
+#if (SIZEOF_INT_P == 8) && !defined(RG_SDL_WINDOW_POINTER)
         /* SDL_Window is a native pointer. On 64-bit system, native pointers
          * should have more than 32-bit values. Windows HWND and X11 Window handles
          * are always in 32-bit values.
